    {
      "version": "0.3.6",
      "seq": 30699,
      "date": "2026-10-20T03:59:24Z",
      "created": "2026-10-20T03:55:37Z",
      "kind": "patch",
      "prerelease": false,
      "notes": "- Sources: choose which sources the PU key cycles through and in what order;\n  any key can be set to \"Cycle sources\".\n- Casting: AirPlay, Spotify (guests on your Wi-Fi too) and UPnP/DLNA can be\n  switched on and named on the key page; the radio goes back to its station\n  20 s after a phone stops.\n- Volume: the quietest knob step is now a setting (Sound).\n- Home Assistant: a key can turn lights on/off, set colour, brightness and\n  white temperature, start a scene, script or automation - with \"Try it\"\n  before saving. The radio also announces itself so Home Assistant finds it,\n  for the new Hasler integration (hasler-homeassistant).",
      "channels": [
        "bench"
      ],
      "halted": [],
      "requires_migration": false,
